        {
            "brief": "Timer handle",
            "description": "An opaque numeric identifier returned by <a href=\"/ref/timer#timer.delay\">timer.delay</a>. Pass it to\n<a href=\"/ref/timer#timer.cancel\">timer.cancel</a>, <a href=\"/ref/timer#timer.trigger\">timer.trigger</a>, or <a href=\"/ref/timer#timer.get_info\">timer.get_info</a> to control\nthe timer. Timers are owned by the script that created them and are removed\nautomatically when the script is deleted. A failed creation returns\n<code>timer.INVALID_TIMER_HANDLE</code>.",
            "error": "",
            "examples": "<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">local</span> <span class=\"n\">handle</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">timer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">delay</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"kr\">function</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;tick&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">end</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">timer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cancel</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">handle</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
